<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_frictions" target="mid_east_energy::shipping_bottleneck_inde" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger US–China export controls and component shortages force manufacturers to reroute semiconductor- and hardware-heavy shipments through alternative hubs and transshipment points (including routes via the Gulf/Suez), increasing port congestion and route delays that raise the maritime shipping bottleneck index.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">mid_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_frictions" target="russia_ukraine_conflict::sabotage_espionage_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened export controls and component shortages tied to US–China tech rivalry make legal procurement of advanced chips and sensors harder for Russian forces and proxies, incentivizing theft, clandestine procurement networks and sabotage of supply nodes to obtain or disrupt hardware.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_frictions" target="space_comm_governance::military_service_reliab" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Export controls, component shortages and logistic delays reduce availability of space‑qualified radios, ground‑station hardware and spare payloads, directly degrading uptime, latency and redundancy of commercial links used for military missions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">space_comm_governance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_frictions" target="western_bond_volatility::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Export controls and component shortages heighten counterparty and settlement risk for market makers and dealers, causing them to reduce inventories and widen bid-ask spreads, which lowers sovereign bond market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">western_bond_volatility</data>
</edge>
