<edge source="space_comm_governance::political_intervention" target="mid_east_energy::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Political pressure that forces commercial satellite imagery or comms providers to restrict distribution of regional monitoring data reduces market transparency about production and shipments, raising risk premia and pushing benchmark oil prices higher.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">space_comm_governance</data>
  <data key="d40">mid_east_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_comm_governance::political_intervention" target="russia_ukraine_conflict::sabotage_espionage_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Public political pressure or explicit requests to providers to block or restrict services to one party provokes that party to mount covert cyber and physical operations against provider infrastructure and supply chains to restore capability or retaliate, raising sabotage and espionage incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">space_comm_governance</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_comm_governance::political_intervention" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_stringency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased political pressure (e.g., demands to block or remove foreign space‑communications vendors) leads policymakers to adopt tighter cross‑border controls and procurement rules that are then extended to AI development and trade, raising AI regulatory restrictiveness in the US–China tech rivalry.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">space_comm_governance</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="space_comm_governance::political_intervention" target="western_bond_volatility::sovereign_spread" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">More frequent or forceful political interventions in the space/communications sector raise perceived policy and expropriation risk, leading external investors to require a larger premium over benchmark sovereigns and widening sovereign spreads.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">space_comm_governance</data>
  <data key="d40">western_bond_volatility</data>
</edge>
